==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-touchy.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*:{{rhymes|ʌtʃi}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|touch}} + {{term|-y#Etymology 1|-y}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|touchier|touchiest}}

# {{context|of a situation}} Extremely [[sensitive]] or [[volatile]]; easily [[disturbed]] to the point of becoming [[unstable]]; requiring [[caution]] or [[tactfulness]].
#: ''It is an extremely '''touchy''' situation, with everybody's patience wearing thin.''
# {{context|of a person}} Easily [[offended]]; [[oversensitive]]; [[ticklish]].
#: ''He can be very '''touchy''' when you talk about his cat, so be as tactful as possible.''

====Related terms====
* [[touchy-feely]]<!-- Not properly derived, since “touchy” rarely means “one who touches”. -->

